cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Praxis in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Praxis: the natural scientist's harness for Claude"
abstract: >-
  Praxis configures large language models to do data-driven natural science
  as a small lab of specialist agents running an explicit, falsifiable
  scientific method over real data. A domain-agnostic core (method loop,
  scientist roles, integrity rules, and a provenance-stamped, mechanically
  validated cache engine) is extended by domain packs; it ships packs for
  ground-based gravitational waves (LVK) and pulsar timing arrays (PTA).
